{
  "about": "Which e2e specs a changed file reaches (scripts/affected-specs.mjs; held complete by src/ci.test.ts). A spec is named by its file's stem; a stem also names the files it was split into ('16-view' is 16-view-house.spec.ts too). A path takes the specs of every area it matches, in order: a 'final' area stops there, a 'fallback' one counts only when nothing else matched. 'all' means the change reaches every spec: the smoke specs here, the whole core on CI. 'self' runs the spec that changed. Heavy specs are run by their group only (-g); nightly ones have no test outside @full.",
  "smoke": ["01-boot", "14-hud", "17-stores-orders", "22-xp", "25-button", "37-first-steps"],
  "heavy": {
    "05-budget-and-fallback": "-g \"the walk at\"",
    "16-view": "-g \"<the test of what changed>\""
  },
  "nightly": ["26-counting"],
  "areas": [
    { "name": "documents", "final": true, "specs": [], "paths": ["**/*.md", "docs/**", "plans/**", "tips/**", ".claude/**", "update-v1/**"] },
    {
      "name": "unit tests and what only they use",
      "final": true,
      "specs": [],
